passing over Arctic ice sheets a  commercial satellite sees nothing but a  blanket of white until it captures  protruding from the ice part of a  concrete structure in the middle of  nowhere there's more polar bears than  people it's a barren wasteland there's  ice and mountains but in the middle we  see this strange structure the looks as  if it's some sort of underground bunker  or lair this reminds me of Superman and  the fortress of solitude you know aliens  hiding this you know upload Center for  Superman to figure out where he's from  so the question is what are they doing  there science writer Joe Pappalardo  investigates the image and spots that  the structure has a road leading to a  door anytime you see it a road that  leads into a tunnel no exit you wonder  what are they housing in there what's  actually being held inside of that  facility the structure glimpsed by the  satellite is the entrance to an  underground vault a bunker to be used in  the event of a global apocalypse there  are 15,000 atom bombs in the world  enough to threaten the human race with  extinction the US and other governments  are prepping for a disaster on the scale  of a nuclear holocaust  there's all sorts of ways for life to  end on earth whatever happens the reason  we'll die is starvation we won't die  because of the nuclear fire we won't die  from the fallout as a species  we'll die because we can't grow enough  food to live satellite cameras have  captured the entrance to an apocalypse  survival bunker aimed at saving the  human species turns out that the turn of  the millennium the Norwegians as well as  the United Nations began this project to  build a massive Seed Vault in case  anything really really bad happened to  the planet the vault is currently  storing more than 900 thousand samples  of plant life but it can store up to  four point five million varieties in 2.5  billion seeds this seed vault is like  the Noah's Ark but for plants if a  global nuclear war wipes out most of  humanity the few survivors will have the  seed tools to reinvent basic agriculture  all they have to do is find the bunker
 

